# Known divergence (by design): this test's runTest helper contains a plain SET
# (set client_min_messages, guarded by IF debug) inside its PL/pgSQL body, so
# Tier-1 body analysis rejects its CREATE (the single +ERROR line below). The
# helper is re-seeded directly on the primary per test (postgis_preseed.sql,
# applied by the patched run_test.pl); runTest is defined with a different body in
# another file, so it is renamed per file (patchPostGISConflictingHelpers) to keep
# seeding unambiguous. Seeding is safe here because every call uses the default
# debug => false, so the SET branch never runs through the pooler. Only the
# rejected CREATE remains.
--- a
+++ b
@@ -1,2 +1,3 @@
+ERROR: SET/RESET inside a PL/pgSQL body is not supported: it changes backend session state that the connection pooler cannot track
 #5699|-checking-
 #5711|-checking-
